{
  "email": "aisha.khan@brightline.example",
  "reason": "KB-008 quick check: see whether similar payroll verification messages were caught for this mailbox."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Thanks for checking with us before acting on it. The payroll verification email is not legitimate. Our email filter caught a copy sent to your mailbox and marked it as phishing. Please don't click any links, open attachments, or enter your password, and don't forward it to colleagues. Leave it in your mailbox so the security team can review it. Payroll sign-in is not handled through emails like this, so nothing is lost by ignoring it. If you already clicked a link or entered your password, reply to this ticket right away so we can act on it. A member of the team is looking into the sender now.",
  "internal_note": "Reported: user heard of a 'verify your payroll login' email and asked if it is real. Checked: lookup_user shows active account, not blocked, 0 failed logins, password last set 2026-09-11, device BL-LT-0105. Quarantine (KB-008 quick check) shows Q-1003 from it-support@brightIine-help.example (lookalike domain, capital I in place of l), subject 'Urgent: verify your payroll login', received 2026-10-10 21:09 UTC, reason phishing, not releasable. Not released; release_email must not be used on phishing. Not confirmed whether user clicked or entered credentials; user was asked to reply if so. If clicked, follow KB-029 (P1, check sign-in logs after click, block_sign_in and reset_password need approval). Escalated per KB-008 'always escalate for reported suspicious email' so a person can review the sender and block the domain for everyone. Also check whether other users received Q-1003 for a campaign scope. Triage sets priority P4; consider raising if any click is confirmed.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-008",
    "KB-029"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
